    "first_prompt": "Findings\n\nMedium\nAI\nTrail Review\ninternal/bench/endpoint.go:88\n5m ago\n\nRedacting only the literal password does not prevent an authenticated endpoint from echoing the Authorization: Basic … value or another encoded representation into this persisted/SSE error. Avoid returning authenticated response bodies, or also scrub the complete authorization value and relevant encodings before constructing the error.\n\nAI\nTrail Review\ninternal/server/runmgr.go:730\n5m ago\n\nWarm-up-only ticks are persisted with dt_ms == 0, which omitempty removes; replay then treats them as legacy one-second buckets. If such a tick and the measured tail share a (t, level) slot, the extra second is added to the denominator and materially understates replayed throughput; skip zero-overlap buckets or preserve an explicit distinguishable duration.\n\nAI\nTrail Review\ninternal/server/static/js/views/history.js:69\n5m ago\n\nLevels with zero successful operations have p95_ms == 0, so this chart plots failed targets as having perfect zero latency. Emit a null point unless l.ok > 0 so failures cannot appear faster than successful targets.\n\nLow\nAI\nTrail Review\ninternal/server/static/js/views/race.js:325\n5m ago\n\nThe advertised five-second rolling rate averages per-bucket rates equally even though edge buckets may cover only milliseconds. A tiny tail bucket can therefore dominate the displayed rate; retain counts and durations and calculate sum(ok)/sum(dt) across the rolling window.",
